text\": \"Reject or flag a ration with missing ingredients, invalid quantities, incompatible units, or proportions that do not form a valid mix; do not present an unreliable cost or nutrition total.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Indicate when an ingredient has no usable cost or nutrition data, or when a proposed ration requires more ingredient stock than is available.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-5\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Let users generate a dated feed plan for a pen from its bunk rate, selected ration, and current animal count, calculating planned total quantity and per-animal quantity.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Show each plan's pen, assigned lot or lots, animal count, ration, planned quantity, scheduled feeding time, cost, expected energy intake, date, and status (planned, in progress, completed, or skipped).\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Allow an authorized user to adjust a plan and its status, and make the current plan available for comparison with the eventual feeding activity.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Flag a plan when the pen has no current animals, its count or bunk rate is unavailable, or its ration is invalid; do not generate a misleading quantity.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If a pen contains animals from multiple lots, preserve the pen-level plan and its lot attribution so subsequent consumption can be rolled up to the appropriate lots.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-6\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Let users record a feeding event for a pen and date with lot, ration, planned quantity, actual delivered quantity, and feeding status.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"On save, calculate variance as actual quantity minus planned quantity, calculate feed cost and energy from the ration, record ingredient consumption, decrement corresponding inventory, and roll cumulative feed quantity and cost up to the affected lot or lots.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Display planned versus actual quantity, variance, cost, energy, inventory consumed, and status for the event so users can inspect execution.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Recalculate affected inventory and lot performance metrics when a feeding event is recorded or corrected; avoid applying the same event's inventory decrement or roll-up twice.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Reject or flag an event with invalid quantities, missing pen/ration/lot attribution, or insufficient ingredient stock; do not silently commit inconsistent inventory and consumption totals.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If actual feed differs from plan, preserve both values and surface the variance, including overfeeding or underfeeding, rather than replacing the planned value.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-7\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Let users record a dated weight measurement for a lot with number weighed, average animal weight, total lot weight, and notes.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Retain each measurement as a dated lot time-series entry and show prior readings and the change in weight since the preceding measurement.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Flag missing, nonpositive, or implausible measurement inputs and avoid treating an invalid reading as a valid trend point.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-8\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Calculate and display days on feed, total weight gain, average daily gain, total feed consumed, feed conversion ratio (feed consumed divided by weight gained), cost of gain (feed cost divided by weight gained), and projected ship date for each lot using its receiving, feeding, and weight records.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Refresh affected lot metrics and projected ship date automatically after a feeding or weight event is recorded or corrected.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Use the latest lot weight and target weight to project remaining days at the calculated daily gain; display the resulting estimated ship date alongside the inputs.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When receiving date, weight history, feed records, target weight, or positive weight gain is insufficient, mark affected metrics or ship-date estimates unavailable and explain the missing/invalid basis instead of dividing by zero or showing a misleading result.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Interpreted feed-to-gain as the stated FCR formula (total feed consumed ÷ total weight gain), and projected ship date as current date plus remaining weight to target divided by ADG.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-9\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Provide dashboard views of active lots and pens, head counts, inventory status, ration use, daily bunk rate, planned versus actual feeding, feed consumed and cost, starting and current weights, gain, ADG, feed-to-gain, cost per gain, and energy consumed.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Provide reports that identify highest-feed-consuming pens, best feed-to-gain and highest-ADG lots, most-used rations, plan adherence, over/underfed pens, remaining inventory, and feed cost per unit of gain.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Show best- and worst-performing lots using the displayed performance measures, and make the comparison basis apparent.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Indicate when values are unavailable or based on incomplete data, rather than presenting missing activity as zero performance.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-10\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Provide a feed-to-gain report that compares ADG, FCR, and cost of gain across multiple lots.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Let users filter report results by date range, breed, sex, or pen and update the displayed comparison to match selected filters.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Let users export the filtered report as CSV or PDF, preserving the selected comparison data and filters in the exported result.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Handle an empty filter result or unavailable metrics explicitly; do not produce a misleading comparison or a malformed export.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-11\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Provide clearly identified sample/mock procurement, lot, pen, inventory, ration, feeding, and weight data that supports exercising the system's key workflows and reports.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Provide a yard-level summary across active lots showing total head, average ADG, average cost of gain, and total feed cost.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Recompute the yard summary from the available active-lot data and indicate when there are no active lots or a metric cannot be calculated from the available data.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-12\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Present the proposed solution and architecture with diagrams that show the main data flows and relationships, including procurement/receiving through lot and pen operations and feed-to-gain outputs.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Provide a demonstrable responsive web app covering the described feedlot workflows, with representative sample data and a walkthrough of observable results.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Provide an overview of the prompts used, testing and validation performed, challenges encountered, and a candid assessment of production readiness and remaining gaps.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Provide a go-to-market strategy and analysis for the proposed product offering.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     }\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"spans\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-1\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"An authorized data manager can import or synchronize PO and receiving records containing vendor, costs, head count, weights, and source identifiers. The system validates and stores accepted records and shows import status and record-level results.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"An authorized user can map each PO line to one or more lots and allocate lot animals to pens using source pen IDs, capacities, and current counts. The system preserves links and allocation quantities so a user can trace a pen or lot back to its PO line and receiving record.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system stores source identifiers, import timestamps, vendor/cost/head-count/weight data, lot and pen mappings, and allocation history; downstream feeding and performance records can refer to the resulting lot and pen entities.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system reports missing required fields, invalid quantities or weights, unknown pens, capacity/count conflicts, unmapped PO lines, and duplicate or conflicting source records without silently creating invalid mappings. A failed record does not prevent valid records in the same import from being reported and processed.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Only authorized users can import source records or create and change PO-to-lot and lot-to-pen mappings; other users can view mappings but cannot alter them.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Imports procurement and receiving records into traceable PO-line → lot → pen allocations; a PO line can map to one or several lots, and lots can occupy one or several pens where source data supports it.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-2\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When animal or lot receiving data is imported, the system calculates and displays a target weight and projected market/ship date for the lot using its entry weight, receiving date, target weight, and configured or measured growth-rate assumption.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system retains the inputs and forecast date/weight used so users can see the basis of a forecast and recalculate it when animal, target, or growth-rate data changes.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If entry weight, receiving date, target weight, or a usable positive growth-rate assumption is missing or invalid, the system flags the forecast as incomplete/unavailable and identifies the missing input; it does not present a misleading date.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Authorized managers can set or change target weights and forecasting assumptions; other users can view forecasts.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Forecasts use incoming/receiving animal data plus configured target weight and an available growth-rate assumption; when no usable growth rate exists, the system identifies the forecast as unavailable rather than inventing one.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-3\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"An authorized user can create and maintain inventory items with name, category, quantity, unit, unit cost, dry-matter percentage, energy value, and storage location, and can record receipts, consumption, and adjustments.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system shows opening stock, received stock, consumed stock, adjustments, and closing/available stock for each item, with each movement dated and traceable to its source where applicable.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system projects remaining inventory for daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, six-month, and annual horizons using expected consumption and the configured wastage ratio; users can change the ratio and see updated estimates.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Inventory movements retain quantity, unit, time, movement type, cost where applicable, and associated feeding event or receipt. Projections expose their horizon and wastage assumption.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system rejects invalid units, negative receipts, and malformed quantities; it flags low or projected-to-run-out stock. If consumption assumptions or wastage configuration are unavailable, it marks projections as incomplete rather than reporting them as reliable.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When a proposed movement exceeds available stock, the system warns and prevents an invalid negative balance unless an authorized adjustment/override is explicitly recorded; the resulting balance and override are auditable.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Authorized inventory users can receive stock, adjust quantities, and change wastage settings; operational users can view stock, while feeding actions follow the inventory availability controls.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Inventory projections apply the configured wastage ratio to estimated consumption; recorded actual feeding decrements inventory by the actual quantity delivered and ingredient mix, without adding a second implicit wastage charge.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-4\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"An authorized nutrition or feed manager can create and edit a ration with name, type, ingredients and proportions, intended animal/weight range, and available nutritional targets.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"For a valid ration, the system calculates ingredient-derived cost per pound, dry matter, and energy values and displays the values alongside the ingredient mix.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A user can request a cost-optimization comparison for eligible ingredients and configured nutritional constraints. The system presents the proposed mix, calculated cost and nutrition, and comparison with the selected/current ration; the user chooses whether to save it as a ration.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system stores ration ingredients and proportions, the ingredient prices and nutritional values used for calculations, calculated outputs, and ration versions so existing plans and feeding records retain their original ration basis.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system rejects missing ingredients, unavailable inventory items, negative proportions, invalid totals, or mixes that do not meet required constraints. If no feasible optimized mix exists, it reports that outcome rather than returning an invalid ration.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Authorized users can create, revise, optimize, and approve rations; other users can view approved rations but cannot change them.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Ration optimization means finding the lowest-cost ingredient mix that satisfies configured nutrition and ingredient constraints, not automatically changing an approved ration.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-5\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"An authorized feed planner can generate a dated plan for a pen by selecting its bunk rate, ration, animal count, and planned delivery time. The system records planned quantity, per-animal quantity, expected energy, and total feed cost and sets a plan status.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system displays plans by date and pen and supports the statuses Planned, In progress, Completed, and Skipped. A user can update status as the work proceeds.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Each plan retains its pen, assigned lot or lots as applicable, count used for calculation, ration/version, rate, quantity, time, cost, energy, date, and status, so later changes do not rewrite the original plan basis.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system prevents generation when the pen, animal count, bunk rate, ration, or date is missing or invalid, and flags plans whose requested ingredient quantities exceed available inventory.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If pen counts, ration, or bunk-rate inputs change after generation, the system identifies the plan as needing review and requires an authorized user to regenerate or confirm it rather than silently changing a saved plan.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Authorized feed planners can generate and change plans; feeding operators can view assigned plans and update execution status, but cannot change ration definitions or planning assumptions unless separately authorized.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"A generated plan calculates quantity from the 