ot overwrite earlier readings.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-8\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"After a feeding event or weight reading is saved, the system recalculates the affected lot's days on feed, total weight gain, ADG, total feed consumed, FCR, cost of gain, and projected ship date, and displays updated values.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system calculates days on feed from receiving date, total gain from entry average weight versus current average weight, ADG as gain divided by days on feed, FCR as feed pounds divided by weight-gain pounds, and cost of gain as feed cost divided by weight-gain pounds.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system retains or can reproduce each metric from dated feeding and weight records and shows the data period and inputs used for the current lot calculation.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If receiving date, entry/current weight, feeding data, or target weight is missing, the relevant metric is marked unavailable with its reason. If days on feed or weight gain is zero/negative, the system avoids division by zero and does not display a misleading FCR, cost of gain, ADG-based forecast, or ship date.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When a saved source event is corrected, the affected lot metrics and projections update from the corrected history; the system does not leave stale derived values visible.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Users with access to a lot can view its metrics; only authorized users can alter source feeding or weight records that affect those metrics.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Feed-to-gain uses total recorded feed in pounds divided by total lot weight gain in pounds; projected ship date uses current date plus remaining target-weight gain divided by positive ADG, equivalent to receiving date plus projected days on feed.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-9\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"An operator can view active lot and pen counts, animals by lot and pen, inventory status, ration usage, pen bunk rates, planned-versus-actual feeding, total feed and cost, starting/current weight, gain, ADG, FCR, cost of gain, energy, and best/worst lot comparisons where data exists.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A user can identify the pen with greatest feed consumption, lot with best FCR or highest ADG, most-used ration, feeding plan variances/over- and underfeeding, remaining inventory, and feed cost per unit of gain.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Users can open a summary to view the underlying date range and associated lots, pens, plans, or activity records supporting a displayed value.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Dashboard values reflect the latest saved records and distinguish unavailable or incomplete metrics from genuine zero values; comparisons identify the applicable period and basis.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When there is no data for a measure or selected period, the dashboard displays an empty/no-data state rather than a fabricated value. Incomplete or inconsistent source data is identified where it affects a metric.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Users see dashboards and records only for yards and operational data they are authorized to access; financial/profitability details can be restricted to authorized roles.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Dashboards and reports present current operational summaries and lot/pen details from saved procurement, inventory, plan, feeding, and weight records; profitability is shown only to the extent that cost and gain inputs are available.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-10\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A user can open a feed-to-gain report and compare lots by ADG, FCR, and cost of gain for a selected date range.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A user can filter the report by date range, breed, sex, and pen; the displayed lot set and comparison metrics update to match the filters.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A user can export the currently filtered report as CSV or PDF, with selected filters, reporting period, lot identifiers, and displayed metric values included.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The report uses saved feeding and weight history and marks metrics unavailable when required inputs are absent or a calculation is undefined.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Invalid date ranges or unsupported filter values are rejected or clearly reported without silently returning an unfiltered report. If filters match no lots, the report and export show an empty result rather than unrelated data.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Users can report and export only data for yards and lots they are authorized to access; financial metrics follow the same access restrictions as other profitability data.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"The report compares per-lot metrics for the selected date range and applies breed, sex, and pen filters to lots/animals represented in that period; export contains the filtered results currently shown.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-11\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"An authorized user can load or reset sample data containing representative procurement/receiving records, lots, pens, inventory, rations, plans, feeding events, and weight measurements sufficient to demonstrate the workflows and metrics.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\